// "Crique Câline": a pirates' cove (issue #19), redrawn after the guide « Conception des circuits »
// (issue #148, docs/GAME_DESIGN.md § 16). Original layout, about 1584 m a lap, turning left round
// the cove: the start straight on the boardwalk of the beach, 6 m up; two hairpins (left, right)
// and the climb of the cape (a bump on it), a tight corner to the left onto its top, 24 m up (issue
// #223: 12 m before); the risky jump's corner on the cape's edge (a tight corner to the left, its
// inside a drop, that a ramp crosses); down the cape (a bump); the bulge on the cliff path (its
// hidden road straight behind a waterfall, while the road goes round), the corner after it (its
// grass bridge behind a curtain of dune grass); a drop of 7 m off the cliff path, 14 m up, onto the
// beach; the ford across the cove's inlet, under its water; three lacets in the dunes (left, right,
// left) and a tight corner to the right onto the boardwalk. Six big turns (five hairpins and the
// bulge's S), four tight corners of 90°: no long soft curve, one long straight. The pieces of the
// shortcuts (the jump's corner and its landing; the bulge, its corner and their paths) are the
// Coteau Citrouille's (the Corniche Cannelle's, issues #107, #156, #111) mirrored, with other
// covers; the rest is new.
//
// Drawn as a plan of straights and arcs (hairpins of 22 m, tight corners of 18 m), its points every
// 8 m along it (the parameters below follow them).
//
// Format: see src/track/data.rs. Point 0 is the start line; karts drive toward point 1 (north, -Z),
// then turn left. The grid sits on the straight behind point 0.
(
    name: "Crique Câline",
    // Dressing (issue #11): the beach (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), the same every time (seed), and
    // pieces placed by hand: pirate flags at the start line (beyond the posts of its arch, issue
    // #79), a watch tower by the grid, a pirate ship run aground on the beach by the ford.
    biome: "Plage",
    // Issue #104: its music (`assets/data/music.ron`).
    music: "sunny-city",
    decor_seed: 7,
    // Issue #211: the beach's terrain (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), and it hugs the road: the cape,
    // 24 m up (issue #223), the cliff path and the boardwalk stand on sand and rock up to their
    // walls, which fall away from them (`embank`, rise over run: about 31°), instead of the skirts
    // down to the beach. The voids stay (the jump's corner, the drop's foot: 6 m under the road at
    // least); the ford keeps its ground.
    terrain: (height: 34.0, scale: 120.0, cliffs: 0.4, terrace: 7.0, floor: 0.15, rise: 35.0,
              rock: (0.64, 0.56, 0.44), steep: 0.8, embank: 0.6),
    // Issue #223: the cape 24 m up (12 m before): from its climb, one saw over the beach's low
    // headlands (28 m at their lowest); a second ring of them behind, higher, closes the horizon.
    far_decor: [
        Range(distance: 560.0, depth: 200.0, height: (50.0, 104.0), spacing: 64.0,
              color: (0.66, 0.54, 0.40), top: ((0.36, 0.62, 0.32), 55.0)),
    ],
    props: [
        (model: "pirate-kit/flag-pirate", at: 0.0, side: Both, height: 4.0, radius: 1.0, gap: 1.8),
        (model: "pirate-kit/tower-complete-small", at: 198.435, side: Right, height: 8.0, radius: 2.4, gap: 1.0),
        (model: "pirate-kit/ship-pirate-small", at: 131.000, side: Right, height: 9.0, radius: 6.0, gap: 46.0),
        // Issue #191: a giant palm in the middle of the bulge, as on the Coteau Citrouille (its
        // pine, mirrored): 8 m from the wall, off the chase camera's sight lines out of the turn.
        (model: "pirate-kit/palm-detailed-straight", at: 90.216, side: Left, height: 22.0, radius: 3.8, gap: 8.0),
    ],
    checkpoint_spacing: 25.0,
